# Force LF regardless of platform/core.autocrlf for anything executed via a
# Linux shebang (inside Docker builds, on EC2, or on an airgapped Linux
# target) — a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true otherwise silently
# rewrites these to CRLF, which breaks the shebang line at exec time
# ("<script>: not found", not an obviously-line-ending-related error).
# Found via a real failure: deploy/scripts/build_and_test_ner_translate_gpu.sh
# uploaded from Windows to an EC2 instance and invoked directly (not via
# `bash script.sh`) failed with exactly this error.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
